1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Give your agents a goal.
Keep the whole operation in view.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:15,000
You choose how the team works.
One goal: maximize cash in the final market.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:23,000
The comparison to run.
Same task and model; change only worker context.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Each team works in parallel.
Three specialists check the market, legality and timing.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Results come back to the Chief.
A returned report is still waiting for verification.

6
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Check the decision before acting.
Every team must pass the same quality checks.

7
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:57,000
The verified decision changes the game.
Cash changes only after the rules accept the sale.

8
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:06,000
One success is not enough.
Repeat on different inventory, prices and tax.

9
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:22,000
New state. The same workflow.
Both teams receive identical starting conditions.

10
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Keep the comparison fair.
Include the Chief, verifier and every worker.

11
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:51,000
No measured token saving yet.
Provider receipts are required before showing a percentage.

12
00:01:51,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Keep control of your agents.
Save the workflow. Validate its cost before reuse.
